# scratch: proof runs materialise a ref here, so this tree holds WHOLE COPIES of test files (measured
# 2026-10-09: 879 *.test.ts under four .scratch dirs). Two things went wrong while it was unignored: a
# `git add -A` swept an in-flight doc edit into an unrelated commit (amendment 196's record landed inside an
# M5 commit and described a tree that did not exist), and a root-level vitest run would have graded
# last week's code and reported it as this tree's result. `conftest/`ed by the 2026-11-09 consolidation:
# main's line uses `.scratch/` deliberately for AN INVESTIGATION record that §192 requires travel with the
# repository, so a blanket ignore would have displaced evidence. The 2026-11-09 merge subtracts from the
# ignore for exactly those tracked files — they stay tracked and ignored-looking, and a git add -A keeps them
# as they are (git does not re-add ignored tracked files). Never untrack a .scratch/ file with this line.
.scratch/

# vitest's config loader writes a TIMESTAMPED bundle next to the config it compiles
# (`apps/studio/vitest.config.ts.timestamp-<ms>-<hash>.mjs`) and does not remove it. Measured 2026-10-20.
vitest.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs

# another tool's own memory directory, which holds no part of this project's build.
.workbuddy-ai/

# scratch scripts and commit-message drafts (amendments 196 and 215 each record the hazard).
tmp_*
commit_msg.txt

# the mutation probe's per-process scratch box (v531).
.nexus-mut-probe*/

# the lanes' scratch directory and the console captures a test run leaves at the root (v606).
.nexus-tmp/
run-result.txt
test_output.txt
test-output.txt

# Three root-level SCRATCH files that were tracked before the rules above existed, and were kept
# tracked by the same `git add -A` hazard the .scratch/ note describes. Measured 2026-11-09 while
# consolidating the tree after the two lines merged:
#   merge_out.bin        — the raw output of a `git merge` that hit add/add conflicts. It is a
#                          transcript of a past event, not a source file, and nothing reads it.
#   .msg.txt             — a commit-message draft for an increment (v590) that has long landed.
#   progress_summary.txt — a status snapshot from v623. The repo is past v643, so the file states
#                          a version that no longer exists: a stale summary in the root is worse
#                          than none, because a reader believes it.
# They are UNTRACKED here but kept on disk (git rm --cached, not git rm): the history keeps them,
# and the working tree loses nothing. This repo's convention is to move a record into docs/ or
# leave it where it is — never to destroy one silently.
merge_out.bin
.msg.txt
progress_summary.txt
